      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\n`CutlassExpertsFp4` claims device capability family 110, so NVFP4 MoE auto-selection picks\r\n`VLLM_CUTLASS` on sm_110 (Jetson AGX Thor) and faults in `profile_run` instead of falling\r\nback to Marlin.\r\n\r\n110 has been in this predicate since #33417 normalised it from\r\n`has_device_capability((10, 0))`, a `>=` check that sm_110 already passed. That PR was about\r\nSM120 and was tested on an RTX PRO 6000. Doesn't look like 110 was ever tried on Thor.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- NVFP4 MoE auto-selection on sm_110 reaches a backend that works instead of one that faults.\r\n- Scoped to the MoE predicate. Dense NVFP4 (`cutlass_scaled_mm_supports_fp4`) is untouched\r\n  and still works on sm_110.\r\n- No behavioural change elsewhere: sm_100 and sm_120 evaluate identically.\r\n- No regression in `tests/kernels/moe/test_cutlass_moe.py`.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nJetson AGX Thor, sm_110, 20 SMs, 122.8 GiB unified.\r\n\r\n`CutlassExpertsFp4._supports_current_device()` returns True before, False after. Checked\r\nagainst 837e87e1c5.\r\n\r\nBefore, serving `RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4` (512 experts):\r\n\r\n```\r\nError: Failed to initialize the TMA descriptor 700\r\nRuntimeError: run_fp4_blockwise_scaled_group_mm_sm100,\r\n  csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/fp4/nvfp4_blockwise_moe_kernel.cu:410,\r\n  Failed to initialize GEMM: status=7 workspace_size=261120\r\n  num_experts=512 M=81920 N=1280 K=2560\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter, the run gets through load, `profile_run` and KV alloc, then stops at an unrelated QSA\r\nkernel on the same device (#56084). With that one fixed as well it serves: 0 errors, coherent\r\noutput at temperature 0.\r\n\r\nRan `test_cutlass_moe.py` on Thor before and after the patch, no failures either time. The\r\n`[nvfp4]` padded-routes case goes from pass to skip, since the backend is no longer offered\r\non this device.\r\n\r\n### Reproducing\r\n\r\nYou only need an sm_110 device to check the predicate.\r\n\r\nThe serving runs don't reproduce on stock vLLM. That checkpoint is ~126 GiB and the board has\r\n122.8 GiB, so these runs mmap the 47.7 GiB PLE n-gram table from NVMe instead of holding it\r\nresident. It's a lookup table, never a GEMM operand, so it can't affect which backend gets\r\npicked. No upstream equivalent, #54129 was closed unmerged.\r\n\r\nNo sm_110 runner in CI, so no test added and everything above was run on hardware.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n**Root cause.** `select_nvfp4_moe_backend` walks an ordered list and takes the first backend\r\nthat claims support. `VLLM_CUTLASS` sits above `MARLIN`. sm_90 falls through because it fails\r\nthe FP4 check; sm_110 passes and stops there. The fault lands in `profile_run`, after\r\nselection, so there's no retry.\r\n\r\n**Scope.** `cutlass_scaled_mm_supports_fp4(110)` is correct for dense, confirmed by calling\r\n`cutlass_scaled_fp4_mm` on device. Only the grouped kernel is broken, so the MoE predicate is\r\nthe right place to fix it, not the global helper.\r\n\r\n**Tradeoff.** Small shapes do work on CUTLASS here, the 4-expert unit test passes unpatched,\r\nand those now go to Marlin, which is W4A16 and slower on prefill. Taking that: selection\r\nhappens once, before shapes are known, and it faults at real MoE sizes. The failure is\r\nshape-dependent too, at 16k context the same call dies in the torch stable-ABI dispatcher\r\ninstead of TMA init.\r\n\r\n**Why not `--moe-backend marlin`.** It's global, and this checkpoint leaves `mtp.*`\r\nunquantized, so it dies earlier:\r\n\r\n```\r\nValueError: moe_backend='marlin' is not supported for unquantized MoE.   (mtp.py:201)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAuto-selection has to be right because the flag can't express per-layer choice.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR. description\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n",
